## Date and Time Generation
- Use terminal `date` command for generating current dates (MCP time server not available)
- Use format: YYYY-MM-DD for all document filenames
- Current date context: Use `date` command to get accurate timestamps
- For session notes, use format: YYYY-MM-DD-session-description.md
- For code improvement logs, use format: YYYY-MM-DD-improvement-description.md


## Time Server Usage
- Query the terminal `date` command for current date/time when generating filenames
- Use UTC timestamps for consistency (`date -u` for UTC, `date` for local time)
- Format dates as YYYY-MM-DD for file naming
